/T (Joe E.)
/Contents (Friedel et al. \(2011\) also acknowledges the limits of the impact of LiH \(and lithium as a whole?\) due to the low primordial LiH abundance of Li/H~10^\(-9\) in the solar system. This rarity makes it difficult to detect, and methods such as optical spectroscopy of Galactic stellar atmospheres are cited as having systematic uncertainties. As a possible remedy to the difficulty of detecting Li atomic lines, they set out to instead search for LiH - the 'simplest Li containing molecule'.)
